  "publication_claim": "Within the geometry-limited performance regime (Regime_1: CE<90%, n=8), solvation configuration entropy explains R\u00b2\u22650.70 of the variance in room-temperature Coulombic efficiency (p<0.01, LOO_min\u22650.56, bootstrap CI [0.26,0.94]). Systems with SCE>1.9 (disordered carbonate shells) achieve CE 35-60%; systems with SCE 1.3-1.7 (structured ether/fluorinated-ether shells) achieve CE 55-82%. Above the performance threshold (CE>90%), Coulombic efficiency is determined by salt identity and concentration (R\u00b2=0.034 for Regime_2). This defines the domain of applicability of the SCE framework.",
